{
  "borough": "Barking And Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its siting, design, mass and bulk,&nbsp;would appear at odds with the prevailing character of the semi-detached pair, appearing as an extension in its own right rather than a dwellinghouse. It would disrupt the built form of the semi-detached pair, resulting in a terracing effect and compromising the design and character of the area. It would present a substantial massing which would not sympathise with the original building lines. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies SP2 and DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The proposed development fails to demonstrate that the proposed off-street parking would have safe and independent access or that additional parking demand could be accommodated in the surrounding area. The proposal therefore provides insufficient evidence to show that it would not cause harm to highway safety.&nbsp;The proposal&nbsp;fails to comply with the following policies which seek to ensure that proposals mitigate impacts to transport networks:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policy&nbsp;T1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
